OLD:
```dart
final step = await iterator.next().toDart;
if (step == null || (step.done?.toDart ?? true)) break;
final handle = step.value;
if (handle == null) break;
``

NEW:
```dart
final step = await iterator.next().toDart;
if (step.done?.toDart ?? true) break;
final web.FileSystemHandle? handle = step.value;
if (handle == null) continue;
``

Changes: (a) `step == null` check dropped (typing under new web stubs — `next()` non-nullable now); (b) a null handle now `continue`s instead of `break`ing — behavioral: skip a null-handle entry and keep listing rather than truncating the list. That's arguably more correct (a null handle shouldn't kill the whole listing). It's a web-only (dart:typed_data/web) OPFS iterator typing adaptation to the 3.50 web stubs. `continue` is strictly more robust. Fine.

